{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments ["<b>And if water be put upon seed</b> etc. From here the Rabbis of blessed memory derived that water prepares (food) to receive impurity; and once water has fallen upon the fruits, they are permanently prepared to receive impurity even though the fruits are dry. And the reason for this is that moisture causes the filth of impurity to adhere; and if we were to decree impurity upon moist things but not upon dry things, you would make your words subject to measurement (i.e., half-measures); and it is not fitting that we decree impurity by halves. Therefore the Torah decreed impurity upon the fruits even though they are dry now, since they were once moist."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:24:52.047319831Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}